---
import { SITE_NAME } from "@/lib/site";
---

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
  <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-muted">About</p>
  <h1 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-ink">
    A directory that checks
  </h1>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-prose space-y-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
    <p>
      {SITE_NAME} is a local business directory for New Jersey, New York, and Pennsylvania,
      built by a small team that has spent years doing web and marketing work for local
      businesses across the same three states.
    </p>
    <p>
      That work taught us two things. First: the difference between a good local business and a
      bad one is enormous, and almost none of it shows up in a star rating. Second: the
      directories people actually use don't check anything — anyone can buy a listing, and
      "verified" usually means a credit card cleared.
    </p>
    <p>
      So the rule this directory is built on is simple: <strong class="text-ink">badges must
      mean something a stranger can check.</strong> When a listing here says a license is
      verified, it names the official state registry we looked it up in and the date we looked.
      When a placement is paid, it says so. When we don't have enough data to say something
      honestly, we say "not enough data" instead of making it up.
    </p>
    <p>
      We're starting small — a set of launch counties in each state where we can verify
      businesses properly — and expanding only as fast as the checking allows.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12 rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-6" aria-labelledby="disclosure-heading">
    <h2 id="disclosure-heading" class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink">
      Disclosures
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 max-w-prose space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <li>
        {SITE_NAME} is operated by a web-design and marketing agency. Some listed businesses
        are agency clients — those listings are always labeled as sponsored and receive no
        ranking benefit. The full rules are in our
        <a href="/editorial-policy" class="font-medium text-brand underline underline-offset-2">editorial policy</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Some copy on this site is drafted with AI assistance and reviewed by a person before
        publishing. Verification decisions — license checks, badges, listing status — are
        always made by a person against the source registry.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</article>
